<%# Sanctioning Author: the last of the five name-author fields to come off
    the vendored typeahead.js/Bloodhound widget. With it goes the shared
    Bloodhound source all five drew on
    (typeaheads/for_name/authors_by_abbrev_bloodhound.js) - nothing else
    used it.

    Label, title, dom ids and param names are unchanged, so the JS that
    keys off them (app/views/names/update.js.erb writes back into
    input#sanctioning-author-by-abbrev) and the server-side resolution
    (Name::AsEdited#resolve_author(params, "sanctioning_author")) carry on
    untouched, including the typed-exact-match-without-a-pick case.

    No dependents_field: unlike the other four author fields, the old
    sanctioning wiring never called window.setDependents after a pick, so
    there is nothing to mirror here.

    wrapper_class "author" brings this field into line with the other four.
    The old markup was the odd one out in leaving the class off, which left
    its label a different colour (see .author in
    stylesheets/utilities/colors.css). %>
<%= render "shared/autocomplete_field",
           f: f,
           id_attribute: :sanctioning_author_id,
           input_id: "sanctioning-author-by-abbrev",
           input_name: "name[sanctioning_author_typeahead]",
           input_value: @name.sanctioning_author.try("abbrev_if_possible"),
           label: "Sanctioning Author",
           title: "Authors will be suggested as you type, so please select from the list or type enough to identify a single author by abbreviation.",
           url: authors_typeahead_on_abbrev_path(format: :html),
           wrapper_class: "author" %>
